  "invariants_checked": [
    "All 325 baseline files in internal/application/service with basename < 'local_' (agent_*, artifact_*, audit_*, auth*, auto_tag_*, automation_*, builtin_skills/agent-browser/SKILL.md, chat_*, chunk*, clear_state*, context_*, data_source_*, datasource_*, desktop_*, dingtalk_*, document_*, embed_*, evaluation*, export_*, extract*, faq_*, feishu_*, file_*, graph*, helper_*, image_multimodal*, im_*, import_*, index_*, inline_*, invitation_*, kb*, knowledge*) were audited line-by-line with zero skimming across multi-tenant/cross-workspace share/API-key isolation, transactional & async compensation correctness, concurrency/context/memory bounds, and GENYEE rebrand hygiene.",
    "Inactive, disabled, or suspended workspaces are fail-closed across background execution paths: scheduled/webhook AutomationRunner.ownerContext, delegated AgentCollaborationService.workerContext, and asynchronous DataSourceService.ProcessSync cancel or reject runs unless an explicit system-admin cross-tenant override applies.",
    "DataSource CRUD, credential mutation, resource browsing, manual sync, pause/resume, and sync-log inspection enforce non-zero caller tenant binding, reject narrowed API-key scopes (APIKeyScopeAgent), and verify syncLog.DataSourceID == payload.DataSourceID and ds.TenantID consistency in ProcessSync.",
    "Organization Agent shares (CustomAgent IDs are composite PK (id, tenant_id)) filter ListSharesByAgent and ShareAgent duplicate-recovery by SourceTenantID == tenantID and guard nil preloaded share.Agent; ShareKnowledgeBase duplicate-share overwrite enforces existingShare.SourceTenantID == tenantID and canManageShare.",
    "KnowledgeBase destructive/config mutations (DeleteKnowledgeBase, SetEmbeddingModel) enforce safe TenantIDFromContext, AuthorizeTenantAPIKeyKnowledgeBases, and owner-workspace checks (blocking org-shared Editors from deleting the owner workspace's KB); CopyKnowledgeBase preserves non-default IndexingStrategy (including Wiki-only KBs), WikiConfig, ExtractConfig, QuestionGenerationConfig, ASRConfig, AutoTagConfig, FAQConfig, ProfileConfig, and VectorStoreID; ProcessKBDelete resolves per-KB custom storage backends and resource-catalog bindings before deleting source files and extracted images and skips empty EmbeddingModelID entries.",
    "Shared-KB storage resolution (buildStorageConfig, resolveFileService, resolveFileServiceForPath, checkStorageEngineConfigured) resolves the KB owner workspace's Tenant via tenantRepo when ctx carries a shared caller's TenantInfo; CloneChunk and cloneFAQKnowledgeBase read source images via source-KB storage resolution so cross-backend clones succeed; Lite-mode (nil Redis) KB clone and knowledge move progress use sync.Map fallback without panicking, FAQ Lite progress deep-clones structs to eliminate -race data races, cleanupKnowledgeResources handles missing TenantInfo without mutating shared Tenant pointers, and reserved metadata keys (_knowledge_transfer, process_overrides) are stripped from user metadata inputs.",
    "FAQ operations (ListFAQEntries, UpdateFAQEntry, SearchFAQEntries, GetFAQEntry, ExportFAQEntries, ExportFAQEntriesJSON, UpsertFAQEntries, GetFAQImportProgress) enforce KB-scoped tag validation (validateFAQTagScope), shared-KB read grants + API-key KB scopes, caller taskID tenant/KB validation, failed-Enqueue EntriesURL blob cleanup, OnlyRecommended search forwarding, and idempotent Completed status preservation on duplicate ProcessFAQImport delivery.",
    "EvaluationService and ChunkService replace MustTenantIDFromContext panics with fail-closed tenant/grant checks, cap in-memory terminal evaluation tasks, enforce writableChunk before GetChunkRevision in RevertDocumentChunk, bind execution tenant in syncChunkIndex/DeleteGeneratedQuestion, and skip vector index deletion on non-embedding (Wiki-only) KBs.",
    "Async compensation and resource bounds: DataTableSummaryService.cleanupOnFailure uses context.WithoutCancel while preserving UpdateKnowledgeForTransfer CAS fencing on moved documents and keeping ParseStatusProcessing while retries remain; ImageMultimodalService bounds stored/local image reads by GetMaxFileSize and rolls back unindexed SQL chunks on BatchIndex/model/engine failure so Asynq retries cleanly; enqueueSummaryRefresh preserves existing completed summaries on pre-enqueue validation errors and RequestKnowledgeSummaryRefresh enforces loadKnowledgeWrite; spanTracker cleans starts entries on SkipSpan/FinalizeAttempt/AbortAttempt; ArtifactCollector.hashStoredArtifact bounds reads to MaxFileBytes; DispatchEmbedWebhook protects envelope fields from payload spoofing and bounds response drains; zero legacy brand/key-prefix residues or host paths exist in the slice."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "W3-SVCA-01",
      "severity": "P1",
      "file": "internal/application/service/automation_runner.go, internal/application/service/agent_collaboration.go, internal/application/service/datasource_service.go",
      "summary": "Background execution paths (AutomationRunner.ownerContext, AgentCollaborationService.workerContext, and DataSourceService.ProcessSync) did not check tenant status ('inactive'/'disabled'/'suspended'), allowing scheduled automations, sub-agent delegations, and connector syncs to keep running for suspended workspaces; DataSourceService methods also lacked service-layer API-key scope and zero-tenant guards and did not verify syncLog.DataSourceID == payload.DataSourceID.",
      "regression_test": "TestAuditW3A_InactiveWorkspaceBlockedInBackgroundPaths",
      "commit": "9f293943815657c266d19c1451babc359d93dfb5"
    },
    {
      "id": "W3-SVCA-02",
